# evals-locks/planner-defects.sha256 — committed copy of the locks of ~/LENSIQ-field/evals/planner-defects/ (owner rule 2026-11-13). Append-only.
# planner defects (owner report 2026-11-18, Samsung Android default browser, planner.html): a ")" alone on the next line in the
# add-person part (a), the start-month <select> cutting "พฤศจิกายน 256(9)" (b), the sticky "หาวันดี" read bar letting faint page
# text show through (c). Widths 360 / 375 / 393 / 412 / 430 × TH / EN / ZH. (a) planner-people-wrap: locked line-wrap probe on
# #plForm, 4 states + 300-440 px sweep; (b) select-fit-kit + 4 parts: every page, the shown text of every shown <select> fits
# (text + padding + border + 24 px arrow), or its full text is visible right under it (.lq-sel-full); planner #plFrom: every
# month must fit in the select itself; (c) readbar-solid: every page with the read bar, 5 scroll positions: background alpha 1,
# body padding >= bar height, no text over/through it, at the bottom no text behind it and the last content above it.
# Locked BEFORE any product change on branch planner-defects (base origin/main b2a6e76c). Trial runs before this lock, used only
# to make the harnesses read correctly (no product file touched): (b) first checked every option of every select (58/229
# failed, mostly long descriptive options that need new wording; narrowed to the coordinator's spec "the selected option text",
# planner #plFrom kept on every option) and one regex escaping fault fixed; (c) "bar shown on planner at scroll 0 at every
# width" changed to "at least once per language" (the read button is on the first 800 px screen at 375 / 393 px).
# Results on main b2a6e76c: (a) 4/4 pass (line-wrap already fixes it; against the pre-line-wrap base 286d813 TH fails with 5
# lone ")" lines); (b) 35 of 229 page × language checks fail (19 pages); (c) 32 of 52 fail (alpha 0.96 on 11 pages).
